## 3. Additional exploration

These go beyond a basic retrieval chatbot.

| Area | What was built | Why |
|---|---|---|
| **Hybrid retrieval** | Semantic search (sentence-transformers all-MiniLM-L6-v2), BM25 keywords and metadata boosts, re-ranked by a cross-encoder (ms-marco-MiniLM-L-6-v2). A hashing fallback is used when the model can't load. | Keyword or vector search alone misses either the exact terms or the paraphrases. |
| **Evidence scoring** | Each answer is labelled Known / Uncertain / Unknown from retrieval scores, topic match and source quality. | The assistant says when it is unsure instead of guessing. |
| **Grounded answers + citation guard** | Every step cites a help article or resolved ticket. Uncited or unsupported steps are removed, including from LLM output. | Limits hallucination. |
| **Adaptive retry** | If the customer says "No", the next attempt uses different evidence and never repeats earlier steps. After 3 attempts the chat goes to a person. | Customers don't get the same answer twice. |
| **Robust classification** | Word-stem and in-order phrase matching, typo correction ("disconnceting" → "disconnecting"), context rules (travel abroad → roaming), chat memory for follow-ups and topic changes. | Real customers write short, misspelt, casual messages. |
| **Scope guard** | Greetings get a greeting; non-telecom questions get a polite sorry message. | Keeps the assistant on topic. |
| **Customer vs agent wording** | Each article has "Resolution steps" (staff) and matching "Customer steps" (plain language). The reply opens with a line built from what the customer said ("Since you've already restarted the router, you can skip that step"). | Customers never see internal jargon. |
| **Human handoff** | Bot → waiting → agent → closed states; queue position; live 3-second updates in both the customer chat and the admin inbox; the bot stays silent while an agent is in the chat. | A smooth customer ↔ admin conversation. |
| **Human-approved learning** | Confirmed fixes and agent fixes go to a review queue. Approval publishes a KB article, appends a dataset row, teaches the classifier the wording and notifies the customer. Nothing is learned automatically. | The system improves without unverified knowledge creeping in. |
| **Agent reply cleaning** | Greetings, the customer's name, questions and sign-offs are stripped. "I've reissued your e-SIM" becomes the staff step "Reissue the customer's e-SIM profile." and the customer step "We'll reissue your e-SIM profile." | Approved articles read like articles, not chat logs. |
| **Emerging issue detection** | Unknown questions are clustered by meaning and shown as Trending problems. A reviewer can turn a cluster into a new issue type plus article. | New problems surface before they become common. |
| **Microservice split** | One codebase runs as a single process or as gateway + nlu + retrieval + generation services, with token-protected internal APIs. | Each AI stage can be scaled or deployed separately. |
| **Security** | Staff sign-in (PBKDF2 hashing, signed tokens, lockout after failed attempts); every admin endpoint requires a token; secrets only in `.env`. | Customers can't reach admin data. |
| **Voice input** | Browser speech recognition in the chat and in "Test the assistant". | Hands-free input. |
| **Honest evaluation** | Separate test and practice question sets, seeded wording variants, Wilson 95% lower bounds, and a leakage check. | Scores aren't inflated (see section 4). |

