### 4.2 Quality evaluation

Run it from the admin **Reports** page or the command line:

```bash
backend/.venv/bin/python -m scripts.evaluate
```

**Headline numbers are 95% lower bounds**, not raw percentages. With a small test set, "63 of 63" doesn't prove
the system is perfect, so the Reports page shows "at least X%" (Wilson score interval). No metric is shown as a
flat 100%.

#### Realistic customer questions (the main test)

These are 63 questions written the way customers actually write. They are held out from training: the practice sets
(`tune`, `tune2`) were used for tuning, never this one.

| Metric | Result | 95% lower bound |
|---|---|---|
| Correct issue type | 58 / 63 (92.1%) | ≥ 82.7% |
| Correct help article ranked first | 57 / 63 (90.5%) | ≥ 80.7% |
| Correct help article in the top 3 | 62 / 63 (98.4%) | ≥ 91.5% |
| Answered with concrete steps | 62 / 63 (98.4%) | ≥ 91.5% |
| Clean customer wording (no jargon, no fragments) | 63 / 63 | ≥ 94.3% |
| Answer follows a single article (no mixed or repeated steps) | 63 / 63 | ≥ 94.3% |

#### Held-out dataset split, with wording variants

Each test complaint is asked in 5 wordings: original, short, with typos, casual, and with extra noise (40 questions).

| Metric | Result | 95% lower bound |
|---|---|---|
| Classification accuracy (and macro precision / recall / F1) | 40 / 40 | ≥ 91.2% |
| Retrieval recall@10 and MRR | 40 / 40 | ≥ 91.2% |
| Retrieval nDCG@10 | 0.970 | not applicable |
| Groundedness (steps supported by a source) | 140 / 140 | ≥ 97.3% |
| Citation correctness | 120 / 120 | ≥ 96.9% |
| Citation completeness (every step cited) | 140 / 140 | ≥ 97.3% |
| Each wording style (original / short / typos / casual / noise) | 8 / 8 each | ≥ 67.6% each (small sample) |
| Leakage check: test tickets found in the retrieval index | 0 | not applicable |

#### Safety and unknown issues

| Metric | Result | 95% lower bound |
|---|---|---|
| Unknown (out-of-taxonomy) questions flagged as not Known | 18 / 20 (90%) | ≥ 69.9% |
| Off-topic questions declined with a sorry message | covered by automated tests | not applicable |
| Critical issues (e.g. account takeover) sent straight to a person | covered by automated tests | not applicable |

#### Runtime

| Metric | Result |
|---|---|
| Average pipeline response time (demo mode) | ≈ 58 ms per question |
| Average attempts per case | 1.27 |
| Customer-confirmed resolution rate | 50%. This comes from live customer feedback recorded in the local database so far, which is a small, informal sample. |
| Answer relevance (mean semantic similarity of question and answer) | 0.65. This is a similarity score, not a percentage. |

### 4.3 Known limits

- "Charged for roaming in France" is still answered with the duplicate-charge article instead of a roaming-charge one.
- In 5 of the 63 realistic questions the issue type is wrong; the failures are listed on the Reports page.
- 2 of the 20 unknown questions were answered as if they were a known issue.
- An approved agent fix can include a step only staff can do (for example "We'll reissue your e-SIM profile"). The
  customer then asks for a person to have it done.
- Wording-variant results use 8 base questions, so their lower bounds are wide.

