## 5. Dataset

All data is **synthetic**, generated to look like real telecom support traffic. It contains no real customer or
operator data, and every ticket is tagged `[synthetic case …]`.

| File | Contents |
|---|---|
| `data/telecom_support_adaptive_60000.csv` | **60,000 tickets**, 32 columns, 30 issue types in 8 categories. Splits: development 48,000 / calibration 6,000 / held_out_test 6,000. The splits are intent-disjoint, so test tickets never appear in the retrieval index. Rows approved by reviewers are appended with ids `TELCO-LIVE-…`. |
| `data/tickets.csv` | A small demo subset, used by the automated tests |
| `data/knowledge_base.csv` | 42 seed help articles, each with Symptoms, Resolution steps, Customer steps, Escalate when and Caution |
| `data/intent_taxonomy.csv` | 30 issue types with keywords, example complaints, category, default product and severity |
| `data/products.csv`, `data/support_categories.csv` | Products (mobile, broadband, 5G, SIM, …) and support categories |
| `data/eval_realistic_complaints.csv` | 63 realistic test questions with the expected issue type and article (held out) |
| `data/tune_realistic_complaints.csv`, `data/tune2_realistic_complaints.csv` | Practice sets used for tuning (64 + 55 questions) |
| `data/eval_unknown_complaints.csv` | 20 out-of-taxonomy questions for unknown-issue detection |
| `data/candidate_cases.csv` | Example review-queue items |

**Ticket columns:** `record_id`, `ticket_id`, `customer_id`, `dataset_split`, `customer_complaint`, `category`,
`intent`, `product`, `severity`, `sentiment`, `language`, `interaction_mode`, `channel`, `entities_json`,
`conversation_context`, `previous_troubleshooting`, `retrieval_text`, `resolution`, `resolution_attempt`,
`resolution_status`, `evidence_status`, `evidence_score`, `citation_source_id`, `citation_type`, `customer_feedback`,
`human_verification_status`, `knowledge_state`, `emerging_class_signal`, `escalation_required`, `source`,
`source_type`, `created_at`.

**Keeping evaluation honest:** an automated test fails if any training example is too similar to a test or practice
question (Jaccard similarity ≥ 0.5), and the evaluation checks that no held-out ticket is in the retrieval index.
